WEBVTT

00:10.380 --> 00:12.830
Correct. You're comprehending this well.

00:12.960 --> 00:13.630
Oh!

00:14.790 --> 00:16.580
Well then, that'll be all for today.

00:18.040 --> 00:20.710
Seriously? I totally don't get it.

00:22.750 --> 00:23.290
Oh!

00:24.290 --> 00:25.290
What're you doing?

00:25.920 --> 00:27.420
You don't get it?

00:27.420 --> 00:30.790
And you understand it? Let me see!

00:30.790 --> 00:32.170
Hey! No way!

00:33.210 --> 00:34.540
Hey Sajo!

00:34.920 --> 00:36.000
Wanna see mine?

00:36.460 --> 00:37.880
Oh, I'm fine...

00:38.250 --> 00:38.790
Oh!

00:38.790 --> 00:40.420
Sajotchi, you sure?

00:40.420 --> 00:41.540
Shut up.

00:42.290 --> 00:43.580
It was difficult, you know?

00:43.580 --> 00:44.790
Yeah, it was.

00:44.790 --> 00:46.880
Now I'm worried about the next test.

00:48.330 --> 00:50.130
Huh? Going somewhere?

00:50.130 --> 00:51.170
School cafeteria.

00:51.750 --> 00:52.750
Oh...

01:10.080 --> 01:14.040
<b>The Dreaming Boy</b>

01:10.080 --> 01:14.040
<b>is a Realist</b>

01:14.170 --> 01:19.750
Nozoki dasu sora no gourei de omoi kakaeta mama shuppatsu

01:19.750 --> 01:24.460
Me wa au noni kaze de yurete toomawari

01:25.540 --> 01:31.000
Akogare matataki no shutter omoide wa kokoro kazatta

01:31.000 --> 01:36.420
Kono jikan, suki mitai modokashii noni

01:37.460 --> 01:42.330
Hanarete chikazuite akirame kaketa yume

01:42.580 --> 01:48.040
Umaku oritateru hi oikakete mitaina

01:48.040 --> 01:53.460
Joukuu ippai ni natta tsutae kirenai koto

01:53.630 --> 01:59.250
Nazeka iro chigai no kimi no honne surechigatta

01:59.250 --> 02:07.540
Mayotchai sou dakedo sora wa zutto futatsu no kodou

02:07.540 --> 02:10.040
Nando mo tsutaeta

02:10.210 --> 02:16.210
Ao no kanjou kuttsuke tara donna keshiki hirogaru no kana

02:16.210 --> 02:20.880
Irodotta omoi shiritainda

02:27.750 --> 02:30.630
<b>End of First Trimester Commemoration Parfait!</b>

02:30.790 --> 02:35.420
As expected for this time of year.
It's hot outside and I'd rather be inside, but-

02:35.420 --> 02:37.380
Oh, there he is! Sajo-kun!

02:43.040 --> 02:45.540
<b>Morals &</b>

02:43.040 --> 02:45.540
<b>Discipline</b>

02:44.750 --> 02:45.540
Um...

02:45.540 --> 02:47.500
You needed me for something, right?

02:48.250 --> 02:52.040
Otherwise, I don't think we're on the side
of having that close of a relationship.   

02:52.210 --> 02:54.330
What? You think so?

02:54.790 --> 02:56.960
Why is your likability on the higher end like this?

02:57.130 --> 02:59.290
Are you like using paid in-app items or something?

02:59.290 --> 03:00.630
That's not fair, Sajo.

03:00.830 --> 03:02.920
Whoa! Senpai, you don't really
know what that means, do you?

03:03.880 --> 03:07.330
In the first place, if I could buy something like
that in reality, I would've bought it long ago.

03:07.330 --> 03:09.080
I-is that how it is?

03:09.540 --> 03:13.630
I heard from Rin-san. Is your cold all better now?

03:13.630 --> 03:15.540
Oh, yes, it is now.

03:15.750 --> 03:17.710
I see. I'm glad.

03:18.880 --> 03:23.880
About your question from earlier, but there was a reason
that Yuyu purposely called to you to stop by.

03:23.880 --> 03:24.630
Okay...

03:24.920 --> 03:26.710
Let me get straight to the point.

03:27.630 --> 03:29.580
Would you like to join the
Morals and Discipline Committee?

03:29.580 --> 03:30.330
What!?

03:31.750 --> 03:32.580
Yours truly...

03:32.790 --> 03:34.710
Do not have what it takes for that.

03:35.460 --> 03:38.250
As the Morals and Discipline Committee Chair,
I retire the post in the fall,

03:38.250 --> 03:41.830
but we haven't been able to recruit even
one single male student from the 1st and 2nd-years.   

03:42.000 --> 03:44.710
As for the girls' side, there's
a strong sense they've come to have fun.

03:44.710 --> 03:46.790
Their ulterior motives are completely obvious.

03:47.080 --> 03:50.250
Those girls only see the Morals and Discipline
Committee as a status symbol.

03:50.500 --> 03:54.330
And in actuality, even right now,
Ichinose-kun is the only boy we have.

03:54.330 --> 03:55.040
What?

03:55.250 --> 03:59.000
Oh, no, um... Yours truly... I, your humble servant...

03:59.170 --> 04:01.920
At a time like this, it was your face that came to mind.

04:02.210 --> 04:06.330
Just like the time you gave me good advice;
I want you to support the Committee.

04:06.830 --> 04:10.670
But what you're talking about in terms of
regime change is in the second trimester, right?

04:10.670 --> 04:11.500
Yes.

04:11.710 --> 04:14.540
That's why I want you to think about it starting from now.

04:14.920 --> 04:16.000
Uh...

04:19.330 --> 04:22.880
Have I been sought after this strongly
at any time before this?

04:23.960 --> 04:24.960
No, never!

04:25.670 --> 04:26.790
However...

04:27.130 --> 04:29.000
<b>Anpan</b>

04:29.170 --> 04:29.880
Oh!

04:30.040 --> 04:30.630
Oh!

04:31.040 --> 04:32.790
I'm counting on you, Sajo-kun!

04:32.790 --> 04:34.080
What!?

04:34.080 --> 04:34.790
Huh?

04:38.420 --> 04:40.330
Sajo... You bastard...

04:40.330 --> 04:42.170
Hey... You...

04:43.540 --> 04:45.420
Oh no! I'm sorry.

04:46.750 --> 04:47.290
Huh!?

04:47.630 --> 04:49.290
Oh, no, this is...!

04:52.250 --> 04:54.170
So, given this kind of situation...

04:54.790 --> 05:01.380
There is absolutely no way I would be fit to be
a Morals and Discipline Committee member, so...

05:03.710 --> 05:06.210
I will have to firmly refuse this-

05:06.210 --> 05:07.330
Whoa!

05:13.500 --> 05:14.250
Oh!

05:15.880 --> 05:17.170
You know, that's...

05:17.170 --> 05:17.830
Oh!

05:20.000 --> 05:21.250
Wh-what?

05:21.790 --> 05:24.420
Why is just half of your hair all ruffled?

05:24.420 --> 05:25.170
Oh!

05:25.500 --> 05:28.250
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow! You got me! You got me!

05:26.130 --> 05:27.710
Take that!

05:30.380 --> 05:31.500
Oh, jeez!

05:31.500 --> 05:32.630
Stay still!

05:51.880 --> 05:52.750
All good!

05:53.880 --> 05:55.460
Um, Natsukawa?

05:55.460 --> 05:56.210
What...?

05:56.540 --> 05:57.420
Oh!

05:58.500 --> 06:00.580
W-will 5,000 yen suffice?

06:01.420 --> 06:02.170
Oh!

06:02.790 --> 06:04.790
I-I don't want that!

06:11.170 --> 06:14.790
In August, drowning accidents and middle-of-the-night
incidences are more likely to occur,

06:14.790 --> 06:17.670
and there is an increasing trend
of internet dangers via social media.

06:17.960 --> 06:22.710
So, even during summer break,
be responsible as students of this school.

06:19.540 --> 06:21.540
<b>Morals &</b>

06:19.540 --> 06:21.540
<b>Discipline</b>

06:21.710 --> 06:22.880
Huh, I see.

06:22.710 --> 06:25.540
And please regard school regulations as important priorities.

06:22.880 --> 06:24.880
So that's the male Morals and Discipline
Committee member in question...

06:25.830 --> 06:29.960
Now then, there is a note of caution for the summer,
from the Morals and Discipline Committee Chair.

06:26.040 --> 06:29.420
He's the teddy bear-type who has the sense of being
able to mix in with the girls and fit in normally.

06:34.000 --> 06:35.830
I am Shinomiya, the Morals
and Discipline Committee Chair.

06:39.460 --> 06:44.670
Senpai, you're super popular, you know?
Of course, everyone would want to join the Committee.

06:45.460 --> 06:51.880
I assume all students already know this, but
a school visit tour will be held the first week of August.

06:52.170 --> 06:54.790
Just because one is not involved in the event,

06:55.130 --> 06:58.670
that does not mean one should lose their dignity
as a student of Koetsu High School.

06:59.040 --> 07:00.380
"Dignity", huh?

07:01.420 --> 07:03.210
Oh, next up is the Student Council.

07:08.210 --> 07:09.460
<b>Student Council</b>

07:08.420 --> 07:13.750
You know, when looking at her in this way,
Big Sis relatively looks the part. What magic is that?

07:15.330 --> 07:21.130
I sincerely hope this summer break will be
a productive time for my fellow students.

07:21.330 --> 07:25.250
Whoa! Yuuki-senpai, as always, you are
the good-looking guy with the cool sexy voice.  

07:25.540 --> 07:27.420
I can understand why the girls' sigh...

07:37.500 --> 07:38.630
Quiet down.

07:39.130 --> 07:42.630
There is one last thing that must be decided.

07:43.210 --> 07:47.750
Who will help out with the school visit
tour during summer break!?

07:48.040 --> 07:49.460
What!?  

07:50.380 --> 07:54.000
Hmm... If there's no one, then I'll narrow down
the choice of candidates.

07:54.000 --> 07:54.630
Oh no!

07:54.790 --> 07:55.580
Alright!

07:55.920 --> 07:59.420
Those of you who don't have club activities during
summer break, you who go straight home, stand up!

08:07.670 --> 08:10.420
Hmm... I guess it'll be Rock-Paper-Scissors.

08:10.630 --> 08:12.630
C'mon, Sajo, just do it.

08:12.880 --> 08:14.040
Yamazaki. Why, you...!

08:14.040 --> 08:16.460
Oh, Sajo-kun. Do I get the feeling you'll do it?

08:17.580 --> 08:19.540
I'm recovering from an illness, so...

08:19.540 --> 08:20.670
You already got better!

08:20.960 --> 08:23.630
Alright! It's Rock-Paper-Scissors time!

08:23.830 --> 08:27.330
Oh, it's one boy and one girl, so split up and do it, okay?

08:27.750 --> 08:31.080
Tabata... How many months has
it been since we last talked?

08:31.380 --> 08:32.210
Who knows?

08:32.210 --> 08:33.130
Now then let's have a fair-

08:33.130 --> 08:34.460
Let's hurry up and do this.

08:34.710 --> 08:35.420
Sorry.

08:35.420 --> 08:37.500
Rock, paper, scissors!

08:39.000 --> 08:40.420
Well, I'm leaving it to you.

08:40.630 --> 08:43.000
What? But I have stuff like cram school.

08:43.330 --> 08:44.960
No, don't say that after you've lost.

08:47.210 --> 08:49.420
Alright! Ichinose-san wins!

08:49.420 --> 08:49.960
Oh!

08:50.250 --> 08:51.750
It'll be Natsukawa-san for the girls.

08:51.750 --> 08:53.790
Oh... I-I'm sorry.

08:54.290 --> 08:55.330
Don't worry about it.

08:55.330 --> 08:57.500
Oh, it'll be Natsukawa-san, huh...?

08:58.000 --> 09:00.830
You seem a little happy about that. Hmpf!

09:02.380 --> 09:04.960
Hey Tabata. I hear that cram school has been tough?

09:05.670 --> 09:06.750
You know, I'll switch with you?

09:06.750 --> 09:07.380
What...?

09:07.670 --> 09:09.000
O-okay...

09:09.710 --> 09:12.580
Otsuki-sensei. It's fine with me if I do it, you know?

09:12.830 --> 09:18.130
Really? I'd appreciate it if you can do it, Sasaki-kun,
but are you going to be okay with the soccer club?

09:18.290 --> 09:20.920
1st-years don't have things like games, so it'll be okay.

09:21.500 --> 09:22.630
The good-looking guy, huh?

09:22.630 --> 09:24.670
Wow, it's the two people with
the high-ranking facial values.

09:24.670 --> 09:26.920
In other words, does this mean Sasaki-kun is...

09:29.460 --> 09:30.750
Tabata-kun, is that okay?

09:30.750 --> 09:32.250
Oh... Yes.

09:32.250 --> 09:37.080
Well, I'm the one who brought it up anyway.
Good luck with cram school, Tabata.

09:37.080 --> 09:38.630
Y-yeah...

09:39.040 --> 09:41.210
Wow. As I'd expect, from a good-looking guy.

09:41.670 --> 09:43.330
Looking forward to working with you, Natsukawa.

09:43.330 --> 09:45.330
Yeah. I'm looking forward to
working with you, Sasaki-kun.

09:45.630 --> 09:49.750
Huh... You know, those two kinda
look great together, but...

09:49.750 --> 09:51.210
Yeah, you're right.

09:51.540 --> 09:52.170
What?

09:52.170 --> 09:53.000
Huh?

09:53.750 --> 09:57.210
Sajotchi... How can you act so normal like that?

09:57.210 --> 10:00.830
Well... I mean, they seem like a good pairing, you know?

10:01.380 --> 10:03.540
Jeez... Loser.

10:07.130 --> 10:09.540
Now then, with this, the first trimester is finished.

10:09.540 --> 10:12.040
Make sure not to forget the next back-to-school date.

10:12.040 --> 10:13.170
Yes ma'am!

10:22.630 --> 10:24.880
Aw, c'mon, give me break.

10:24.880 --> 10:26.080
Huh? What was that?

10:26.080 --> 10:27.210
It's nothing.

10:27.330 --> 10:32.380
Come to think of it, depending on Rock-Paper-Scissors,
it could've been just you and Aichi, you know?

10:32.380 --> 10:34.290
You know, I didn't need to hear that.

10:34.580 --> 10:38.210
You may end up with withdrawal symptoms
because you can't see her during summer break.

10:38.210 --> 10:39.210
Maybe.

10:55.040 --> 10:57.710
Club activities are on a pretty tight schedule, you know?

10:57.920 --> 11:00.420
Basically, my days off are
Saturdays, Sundays, and Obon.

11:01.210 --> 11:03.500
You don't have to overextend yourself
to hang out with me.

11:03.500 --> 11:06.460
Nope! I wanna hang out with you, Aichi.

11:06.790 --> 11:08.750
The ocean and fireworks are a must do!

11:08.960 --> 11:09.750
Jeez...

11:10.210 --> 11:11.580
Sorry to keep you waiting!

11:12.330 --> 11:13.250
Wow!

11:13.250 --> 11:16.380
Alright! End of first trimester commemoration parfait!

11:17.710 --> 11:19.210
Let's eat!

11:21.290 --> 11:25.500
So... Since it'll be the perfect opportunity,
can we invite some other people?

11:25.500 --> 11:27.330
Yeah, that sounds like fun.

11:29.080 --> 11:31.250
Really!? Then...

11:31.580 --> 11:33.040
How about like Sajotchi?

11:33.500 --> 11:37.080
Wh-why is his name popping up here...?

11:37.750 --> 11:39.250
Well, that's, you know...?

11:45.040 --> 11:49.040
<b>The Dreaming Boy</b>

11:45.040 --> 11:49.040
<b>is a Realist</b>

11:50.880 --> 11:51.790
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

11:51.670 --> 11:53.330
<b>Used books</b>

11:51.670 --> 11:53.330
<b>- Buy & Sell</b>

11:52.540 --> 11:55.040
<b>We buy</b>

11:52.540 --> 11:55.040
<b>used books.</b>

11:57.420 --> 11:58.170
Oomph!

12:08.080 --> 12:10.420
Sir, I finished organizing the books!

12:10.920 --> 12:13.380
Already? Really?

12:18.670 --> 12:19.750
Wow...

12:20.210 --> 12:23.630
It was a wise choice that I decided to hire you.

12:24.000 --> 12:27.210
That it would be this different from having
just one more person here, is...  

12:28.170 --> 12:31.080
Although it also probably has something to do
with how you get the hang of things well.

12:31.540 --> 12:34.040
Well, I did do things like part-time
work at convenience stores.

12:34.040 --> 12:38.080
If it's about this amount of workload, then conversely,
I have to be doing something or it's stressful.

12:38.460 --> 12:40.080
Huh, I see.

12:40.080 --> 12:40.960
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

12:41.290 --> 12:45.080
<b>Used books -</b>

12:41.290 --> 12:45.080
<b>Buy & Sell</b>

12:45.080 --> 12:46.420
<b>We</b>

12:45.080 --> 12:46.420
<b>buy</b>

12:45.090 --> 12:46.420
<b>used</b>

12:45.090 --> 12:46.420
<b>books.</b>

12:46.040 --> 12:48.290
Bastard! Hey, stop messing around!

12:48.500 --> 12:49.330
Huh?

12:49.330 --> 12:49.960
C'mon!

12:49.960 --> 12:51.670
Give it back!

12:51.880 --> 12:53.040
You can't reach it, can you!?

12:54.080 --> 12:55.000
Here!

12:56.040 --> 12:57.540
Give it back!

12:56.290 --> 12:58.000
So what!? You're just a shrimp.

12:58.000 --> 12:59.500
C'mon, say something!

12:59.500 --> 13:00.170
Whoa!

13:03.790 --> 13:06.080
Hey! C'mon, stop that!

13:07.170 --> 13:08.960
What the hell, you bastard. You wanna get beaten up!?

13:08.960 --> 13:12.130
Yeah, okay, okay. Jeez, just hit me, will ya?

13:12.380 --> 13:14.630
Aw, man. You okay?

13:14.630 --> 13:16.630
Wh-who the hell are you!?

13:19.170 --> 13:21.500
Are you hurt? Can you stand?

13:28.750 --> 13:30.750
Let's go. You must be stupid.

13:30.750 --> 13:32.420
Stupid, stupid!

13:34.960 --> 13:36.170
Can you say your name?

13:36.380 --> 13:38.420
S-Sasaki...

13:38.750 --> 13:39.540
Huh!?

13:40.670 --> 13:42.170
Kota Sasaki.

13:40.670 --> 13:42.670
<b>Kota</b>

13:40.670 --> 13:42.670
<b>Sasaki</b>

13:42.880 --> 13:48.830
Oh, Sasaki spelled that way, huh? So, Kota-kun,
can you say your home phone number?

13:49.210 --> 13:49.960
Yeah.

13:51.670 --> 13:53.170
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

13:56.330 --> 14:01.250
I see. Well, that must've been scary.
It's okay, you can relax now.

14:01.250 --> 14:02.170
Ko-kun!

14:02.170 --> 14:02.920
Oh!

14:08.710 --> 14:09.670
Big Sis!

14:11.330 --> 14:12.460
Are you hurt?

14:12.460 --> 14:13.420
I'm okay.

14:13.710 --> 14:14.580
Okay then...

14:15.290 --> 14:17.250
Oh! Um...

14:17.460 --> 14:21.670
I am the one who called from here.
My name is Wataru Sajo.

14:22.000 --> 14:25.500
Apparently, he was getting picked on by some
middle schoolers at the underpass over there.

14:25.880 --> 14:31.250
Oh! Um... Thank you very much, Sajo-san.

14:35.250 --> 14:36.130
Oh!

14:36.580 --> 14:39.040
Whoa! She's got that young woman aura!

14:39.290 --> 14:42.960
Soft and floaty! I-is this that female college student thing?

14:43.380 --> 14:45.170
This is a new sensation!

14:46.670 --> 14:47.790
Oh, not at all.

14:48.170 --> 14:52.790
More importantly, please check later that there are no
strange damage marks on his bookbag and belongings.

14:53.420 --> 14:55.710
It would be bad if this was a habitual thing.

14:57.130 --> 14:59.330
Y-yes! I understand.

14:59.880 --> 15:01.920
Kota-kun, have you calm down now?

15:01.920 --> 15:02.630
Yeah.

15:02.830 --> 15:06.880
From next time on, don't go to places that
are kind of deserted by yourself, okay?

15:07.290 --> 15:09.290
Because your older sister will worry.

15:10.250 --> 15:11.420
I'm sorry...

15:12.000 --> 15:15.500
You don't have to apologize.
From next time, okay? Next time.

15:16.250 --> 15:20.670
Lucky for you, Ko-kun.
You got saved by a nice young man.

15:22.420 --> 15:24.330
Oh... Well...

15:28.580 --> 15:30.420
"Young man", huh...?

15:41.330 --> 15:42.580
The usual.

15:42.580 --> 15:44.080
What are you, a regular at a café?

15:44.080 --> 15:44.830
What?

15:44.830 --> 15:46.290
Nothing at all.

15:56.750 --> 15:59.540
You know, to think that this is
our Student Council Vice President.

15:59.540 --> 16:01.000
Shut up, idiot.

16:02.920 --> 16:05.540
Come to think of it, I'm surprised you're awake
even though it's summer break.

16:05.790 --> 16:07.630
Well, the early bird gets the money.

16:07.960 --> 16:11.630
You don't get paid money by the school,
but you get paid money for part-time work, you know?

16:12.210 --> 16:15.290
It's a used bookstore, right? Is it that easy?

16:15.540 --> 16:18.080
The fact it's a privately owned store is the good thing.

16:18.500 --> 16:22.170
Unlike chain stores where the more
you do the more work comes raining down,  

16:22.500 --> 16:25.210
for this one, if you do what you need to do,
then you're done, and so it's easy.  

16:30.750 --> 16:34.040
I see. So, the Student Council was a chain store, huh?

16:34.670 --> 16:35.670
You know that's not true.

16:36.130 --> 16:39.040
Are the preparations for
the school visit tour moving along?

16:39.460 --> 16:41.880
Although it's done jointly with the Morals
and Discipline Committee members,

16:41.880 --> 16:43.210
the Student Council is running it, right?

16:43.210 --> 16:46.880
Don't take me for a fool.
I'm not the Vice President for nothing.

16:46.880 --> 16:49.210
Yeah, okay, sorry about that.

16:52.710 --> 16:56.210
Speaking of, I heard you got invited to be
a Morals and Discipline Committee member?

16:56.210 --> 16:57.290
How did you...?

16:58.580 --> 17:00.380
From Shinomiya-senpai?

17:00.380 --> 17:04.500
Well, something like that. More importantly,
what kind of relationship do you two have?

17:04.500 --> 17:09.130
"Relationship"...? I think it's like
a little brother to a big sis kind of thing.

17:09.500 --> 17:12.500
Huh. Well, you know, not that I mind.

17:13.880 --> 17:19.420
You gonna join the Committee? I know they've been
wanting to increase male members for a long time.

17:19.630 --> 17:21.130
You know there's no way.

17:21.580 --> 17:23.920
No matter how I look at it,
the burden of responsibility is too heavy.

17:24.210 --> 17:26.250
Then you should join the Student Council.

17:27.000 --> 17:28.500
Hey! What the...!?

17:28.500 --> 17:30.290
Huh!? What!? Why?

17:30.630 --> 17:35.500
I don't want to leave the rest and entrust it
to some nobody from who knows where, after all.

17:35.750 --> 17:36.750
Claumati...

17:37.250 --> 17:43.330
As I am the top of the class year, I, Claudine Marika
Shinonome, grant you the privilege of supporting me.

17:43.830 --> 17:47.630
If you incorporate Natsukawa into this,
then you yourself are going to be upstaged instead.

17:48.080 --> 17:49.790
H-how rude!

17:50.460 --> 17:51.210
What?

17:51.210 --> 17:53.960
Well, I am the nobody of the Sajo family, you know?

17:53.960 --> 17:55.580
But you're good at administrative stuff.

17:55.830 --> 17:57.750
Are you saying that's a strength of mine?

17:58.000 --> 17:58.710
Here.

17:59.290 --> 18:02.960
Anyway, the Student Council thing.
I'm relatively serious about it.

18:03.380 --> 18:04.500
So, think about it.

18:05.330 --> 18:10.000
What!? Hang on, you're "serious about it"?
Are you really serious? You're joking, right?

18:12.580 --> 18:15.330
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

18:18.000 --> 18:20.500
"A great masterpiece that
you can't die without having read"...

18:21.290 --> 18:22.710
I guess that's overstating it.

18:22.710 --> 18:26.000
No, if it's not said to this extent,
then it wouldn't be a catchphrase.

18:27.540 --> 18:28.580
Excuse me.

18:29.250 --> 18:31.380
Yes, yes, I'll be right there. Oh!

18:35.000 --> 18:36.750
Hello Sajo-san.

18:37.960 --> 18:39.880
H-hello. It's been a while.

18:40.210 --> 18:42.210
Thank you for your help the other day.

18:42.790 --> 18:48.500
I was flustered at that time, so we ended up going home
right away, but this is a used bookstore, isn't it?

18:49.420 --> 18:51.960
To think there was a store like this near our house is...

18:52.460 --> 18:54.130
Do you live nearby here?

18:54.380 --> 18:58.460
Yes! I am happy I have made acquaintances
with a shop assistant of a bookstore.

18:59.000 --> 19:01.000
I am the one who is happy.

19:01.500 --> 19:04.960
Sasaki-san, I end up getting nervous
because you are so mature.

19:05.380 --> 19:09.920
"Mature"? Oh, but this is the first time
I have been told something like that.  

19:10.380 --> 19:13.920
Up until a little while ago, I was being told
I was childish, for the longest time.

19:14.080 --> 19:16.210
Oh no, you don't seem like that at all...

19:16.210 --> 19:18.920
Hang on, this is going to end up
sounding like sexual harassment.

19:20.880 --> 19:22.830
Are you on your way to your campus today?

19:23.330 --> 19:29.000
No. Oh, but my school does not
have like a campus feel to it.  

19:29.210 --> 19:30.210
Is that so?

19:30.540 --> 19:35.790
Yes. There are only girls, so it does
not have that kind of open-minded feel to it.

19:36.170 --> 19:37.460
And you, Sajo-san?

19:37.960 --> 19:39.630
Do you know of Koetsu High School?

19:40.000 --> 19:42.880
Wow! So, you are a student there.

19:43.420 --> 19:50.130
Koetsu High School is nice, isn't it? And the uniforms
are cute, and it really is like a college campus.

19:50.130 --> 19:52.790
Yeah, it is unnecessarily spacious.

19:52.790 --> 19:57.210
Yes! It is roomy and relaxing,
and I think it is a truly wonderful place.

19:57.710 --> 20:01.080
I see now... It really makes sense now.

20:01.500 --> 20:06.790
Oh no, Sasaki-san, I think you are the one
who combines both a sense of maturity and purity.

20:08.460 --> 20:12.170
That's... Sajo-san, you flatter me too much.

20:12.630 --> 20:13.460
Oh!

20:13.880 --> 20:15.500
What is up with this pureness?

20:15.500 --> 20:17.670
It's so bright I feel like I'm going
to be blown away without a trace.

20:17.670 --> 20:18.830
Once again...

20:18.830 --> 20:23.710
From the other day, in regard to Ko-kun,
thank you very much for saving my little brother.

20:24.750 --> 20:28.330
Sajo-san, just as you told me,
I did check his backpack,

20:28.710 --> 20:32.000
but there weren't any particular marks on it,
so I was really relieved.

20:32.000 --> 20:37.330
Oh... Ah, I am glad to hear that.
How is Kota-kun doing, since then?

20:37.960 --> 20:39.880
Has he been afraid or anything like that?

20:39.880 --> 20:45.630
Sajo-san, I think your presence had a very big influence
on him. He is outside playing again today.

20:46.080 --> 20:47.330
I'm glad for that.

20:49.920 --> 20:50.880
Actually...

20:51.500 --> 20:59.250
This is an embarrassing thing, but I also haven't
talked with a man all that much, so I learned a lot.  

20:59.250 --> 20:59.920
What!?

21:00.500 --> 21:04.540
H-how do I say this? Your family probably
cherishes and takes good care of you then.

21:04.880 --> 21:09.330
That is true, but... If anything,
they are overprotective, so to speak...

21:10.920 --> 21:14.330
Oh, I apologize for having talked
to you for such a long time.

21:17.540 --> 21:20.790
This is to thank you for the other day.
It's just a little something, but...

21:20.790 --> 21:23.500
Oh, I'm sorry, I think I made you
go out of the way to do this for me.  

21:23.500 --> 21:25.210
Not at all! The pleasure is all mine.

21:27.880 --> 21:30.170
I-is it all right if I come here again?

21:30.290 --> 21:32.960
Huh!? O-of course!

21:36.040 --> 21:37.000
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

21:46.920 --> 21:48.920
Given this size, is it a handkerchief, maybe?

21:50.040 --> 21:52.460
Like those elegant ones with lace on them?

21:52.670 --> 21:55.290
No, it's probably a large-sized one for men...

21:58.540 --> 21:59.330
Huh?

22:02.880 --> 22:03.710
Uh...

22:05.420 --> 22:06.540
Do I...

22:07.290 --> 22:08.710
seem childish...?

22:28.580 --> 22:31.040
Mou, shitsukoi! Danante, ne

22:31.330 --> 22:34.630
Aa. Iwanakya yokatta na...

22:35.460 --> 22:41.580
Demo ne nande sona kyuu ni sokkenai kao shite kuruno...

22:43.290 --> 22:45.500
Kidoku no mama oitekebori na message

22:45.500 --> 22:47.790
Demo group dato henshin aru mitai na

22:48.000 --> 22:49.960
Chikai to omottara tooku natte

22:50.210 --> 22:51.750
Nande konna sabishin daro

22:51.750 --> 22:53.630
Kyou wa oikakete... kurenai no?

22:53.630 --> 22:55.170
Sunao ni naretara ii noni

22:56.630 --> 23:02.960
Datte hajimete shitta no konna setsunai kimochi ga aru kototte...

23:02.960 --> 23:04.380
Nanoni, nee!

23:04.380 --> 23:05.920
Doushite itchau no??

23:05.920 --> 23:07.670
Nande naisho nano!?

23:07.880 --> 23:10.040
Modokashii darake de...

23:10.040 --> 23:11.420
Aa! Aa!

23:11.420 --> 23:13.130
Ienai yo konna no

23:13.130 --> 23:17.130
Dakedo sakki wa honne janai kara

23:17.130 --> 23:18.500
Tsutawatte yo

23:18.580 --> 23:20.210
Doushite okotchau no...

23:20.210 --> 23:21.750
Kawaiku dekinai no...

23:21.750 --> 23:24.210
Kirai ni natta no...??

23:24.380 --> 23:27.080
Aa! Aa! A, aa!

23:29.080 --> 23:30.040
Doushite

23:30.710 --> 23:32.000
Kirai ni naranai de

23:35.040 --> 23:36.420
...Kiite, "Anone...!"
